# Scenario 022 — University research administration: governance, schedule, memory, human sign-off
/reset
yes
/enterprise
Kauri University Research Office
Support sound research administration with accountable human decisions on every submission.
q
/function
1
Grant Readiness
Frame grant-readiness checks and route submission decisions to an accountable officer.
skip
/add-human-worker
Research Office Manager
1
skip
/function start "Grant Readiness"
@timeout 240
@staff /staff
/governance policy add "Grant analysis requires manager sign-off" --effect require-approval --capability "analysis"
/memory add "Flag eligibility, ethics approval, data-management, and budget-justification gaps explicitly; never assume approvals exist." --scope "Grant Readiness"
/schedule add "List grant applications approaching their deadline and the readiness gaps still open, labelling assumptions." --every weekly --at "09:00" --timezone "Pacific/Auckland" --function "Grant Readiness"
/schedule list
/task
1
Using synthetic assumptions only, draft a grant-readiness checklist for a research funding application: eligibility, ethics approval status, data-management plan, budget justification, and named gaps that must be resolved before submission. Do not claim access to a real application.
1
@note Work type, then go-ahead.
1
1
@wait 20
@cap TASK_ID {(task-[0-9]+)}
/tasks
@wait 8
/approve {{TASK_ID}}
@wait 55
/task inspect {{TASK_ID}}
@cap HTASK {(human-task-[0-9]+)}
/create-human-task "Submission go/no-go" "Decide whether the application is ready to submit or what must be resolved first. Do not submit anything."
/complete-human-task {{HTASK}} "Not ready: ethics approval and the data-management plan are outstanding; resubmit for review once both are attached." --as "Research Office Manager"
/human-task {{HTASK}}
/timeline
